Recon-PortScan — port scanning. The attacker probes ports to identify open services.

VulnerabilityScan — vulnerability scanning. Checks devices for known security flaws.

Recon-HostDiscovery — host discovery. Identifies which devices are present on the network.

Uploading_Attack — an attempt to upload a malicious file to a device.

SQL_injection — the injection of SQL code into a query to steal or modify data.

CommandInjection — the injection of an OS command to execute it on a device.

XSS — the injection of a JavaScript script into a page to attack the user's browser.

DDoS-ACK_Fragmentation, DDoS-UDP_Fragmentation, DDoS-SYN_Flood, DDoS-TCP_Flood, DDoS-HTTP_Flood, DDoS-PSHACK_Fragmentation, DDoS-ICMP_Flood, and DDoS-SlowLoris are various types of DDoS flood attacks. They all share a single goal: to overwhelm the target and take it offline.

Mirai-greeth_flood and Mirai-udpplain are attacks launched by the Mirai botnet, which infects IoT devices to orchestrate massive DDoS attacks.

MITM-ArpSpoofing involves manipulating ARP tables to position an attacker between two devices and intercept traffic.

DNS_Spoofing involves tampering with DNS responses to redirect a victim to a fraudulent website.

BrowserHijacking involves hijacking a browser session to act on the user's behalf.

